    description: ""  # e170
    fields:  # e170
      statement: "A catalogue row must name the boundary its call actually crosses. VIOLATED: haskell.yaml rows System.Directory's getHomeDirectory and getTemporaryDirectory inside a 14-function fs_read block, but both read ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES rather than the filesystem. getTemporaryDirectoryInternal looks up TMPDIR via lookupEnvOs (Posix.getEnv) and falls back to the hardcoded literal \"/tmp\"; getHomeDirectory looks up HOME the same way, falling back to getpwuid_r. Neither performs a stat or an open on the POSIX path. Confirmed independently three times in this sweep: two workers on different chunks, plus a third reaching the same function through System.Directory.Extra, which re-exports System.Directory wholesale."  # e170
      root_cause: "Module-granularity attribution over a block whose other twelve members genuinely are filesystem reads (listDirectory, doesFileExist, getFileSize, canonicalizePath and so on). The two \"give me a well-known directory\" functions LOOK like directory queries and sit naturally beside them, but the directory they name is supplied by the environment, not discovered on disk. Direction matters here: these should move toward env_read, which is a TIGHTENING (env_read means may-carry-a-credential), not a loosening."  # e170
